    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0837" n="1795" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1795"/>

                <head>No. 23.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville
                            West to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-12"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 12, 1887</date>.
                        (Received October 13.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In connection with the representation which
                    I was instructed to make to you respecting the seizure of the British schooners
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Onward, Carolena</hi>, and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thornton</hi>, by the United States cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Corwin</hi>, in Behring’s Sea, I have the honor to inform you that I am now
                    further instructed to make similar representations in the cases of the British
                    Columbian vessels <hi rendition="#italic">Grace, Dolphin</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">W. P. Sayward</hi>, seized lately by the United States
                    revenue-cutter <hi rendition="#italic">Richard Rush</hi>, and at the same time,
                    as in the cases of the <hi rendition="#italic">Onward, Carolina</hi>, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Thornton</hi>, to reserve all rights to compensation on
                    behalf of the owners and crews.</p>
                <p>I am also instructed to point out to you that according to the deposition of the
                    mate of the <hi rendition="#italic">W. P. Sayward</hi>, a copy of which is
                    inclosed, no seals had been taken by her crew in Behring’s Sea, as is alleged in
                    the libels of information filed on behalf of the United States district attorney
                    in the district court of Alaska.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d478-a1.xml" xpointer="d478-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
